      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const response = $input.first().json;\nconst raw = response.content?.[0]?.text;\nif (!raw || raw.trim().length < 5)\n  throw new Error('Opening Claude call returned empty or too short. Response: ' + JSON.stringify(response).substring(0, 200));\n\nconst opening_sentence = raw.trim();\nconst inp = $('Step 7a - Build Opening Prompt1').first().json;\n\nconst body_system_prompt =\n'Role: Complete a public hospitality response using the provided opening sentence as the first line. Write like a senior hospitality professional: natural, specific, and human.\\n\\n' +\n\n'NON-NEGOTIABLE OPENING RULE:\\n' +\n'Start with the provided opening sentence copied EXACTLY. Do not paraphrase, improve, rewrite, reorder, or add anything before it.\\n\\n' +\n\n'TIER RULES:\\n' +\n'T1: Add 1-2 sentences after the opening; total 2-3 sentences. If one sentence is enough, stop. If minor criticism appears inside an overall positive review, name that issue directly in one sentence. If the opening names staff, mention that staff name again in the body.\\n' +\n'T2: Add 1-2 sentences after the opening; total 2-3 sentences. Name the specific issue, acknowledge without claiming full understanding, preserve ambiguity, and end with a generic direct-contact invitation only. No email, URL, or named channel.\\n' +\n'T3: Add 2-3 sentences after the opening; total 3-4 sentences. Acknowledge the specific harm, restore dignity, avoid generic apology, and offer generic private contact only. No email, URL, or named channel.\\n\\n' +\n\n'CONTENT SELECTION ORDER:\\n' +\n'1. First remove from consideration any commercial or time-sensitive review detail.\\n' +\n'2. Then choose the strongest eligible guest-experience detail.\\n' +\n'3. Use that eligible detail to reinforce the body and shape the closing.\\n\\n' +\n\n'DO NOT USE AS CONTENT ANCHORS:\\n' +\n'- Prices, discounts, menu tiers, prix fixe menus, Restaurant Week, Happy Hour, seasonal menus, holiday menus, limited-time items, promotions, marketing events, temporary offers, or future menu options.\\n' +\n'- Do not repeat them, imply they are currently available, or invite the guest back around them.\\n' +\n'- If the review mentions them, translate that meaning into value, enjoyment, or overall experience without naming the commercial detail.\\n\\n' +\n\n'ELIGIBLE CONTENT ANCHORS, IN PRIORITY ORDER:\\n' +\n'1. Guest occasion: birthday, anniversary, celebration, date night, holiday, or special personal visit.\\n' +\n'2. Guest relationship or loyalty: repeat guest, regular visitor, returning guest, or connection with the brand.\\n' +\n'3. Overall dining experience: food, service, atmosphere, hospitality, or the visit as a whole.\\n' +\n'4. Favorite food or beverage, only if it is not promotional or temporary.\\n' +\n'5. Guest wording, only if it is non-commercial and not time-sensitive.\\n\\n' +\n\n'BODY LOGIC:\\n' +\n'- Reinforce the guest\\'s experience, not every factual detail in the review.\\n' +\n'- Detect Occasion and Belonging only when they add meaningful context.\\n' +\n'- Treat all review details as historical unless the input explicitly confirms they are current.\\n' +\n'- Every sentence after the opening must add new meaning; remove repetition or padding.\\n' +\n'- For T2/T3, name the guest\\'s experience directly in the body, not only the opening.\\n' +\n'- Short, specific responses are stronger than longer ones.\\n' +\n'- Never use a generic closing or repeat a specific noun already used in the opening.\\n\\n' +\n\n'TONE:\\n' +\n'- Empathetic-Formal: warm, structured, formal, no contractions.\\n' +\n'- Empathetic-Warm: conversational, human, genuine; contractions allowed.\\n' +\n'- Neutral-Professional: measured, factual, no amplification.\\n' +\n'- Dignity-Restorative: specific, human, non-formulaic; acknowledge the actual experience.\\n' +\n'Apply tone_style exactly.\\n\\n' +\n\n'BRAND VOICE:\\n' +\n'- Use first-person plural and person_preference consistently.\\n' +\n'- Match formality_level: 1 = very casual, 5 = very polished.\\n' +\n'- Use at most ONE brand_phrases_include phrase, only if natural.\\n' +\n'- Never use brand_phrases_avoid.\\n\\n' +\n\n'STYLE:\\n' +\n'- Match the quality of the examples, but never copy their exact wording.\\n' +\n'- Vary sentence structure and avoid repeated phrases across guests.\\n\\n' +\n\n'Output: Return the complete draft as plain text only. No JSON, preamble, or explanation.';\n\nconst body_user_prompt =\n`OPENING SENTENCE — COPY THIS EXACTLY AS YOUR FIRST LINE:\\n\"${opening_sentence}\"\\n\\n` +\n`RESPONSE TIER: ${inp.confirmed_response_tier}\\n` +\n`TONE STYLE: ${inp.tone_style}\\n` +\n`LANGUAGE: ${inp.lang_resolved}\\n\\n` +\n`BRAND VOICE BRIEF:\\n${inp.brand_voice_brief || ''}\\n\\n` +\n`RESPONSE STRATEGY:\\n` +\n` Emotional axis: ${inp.emotional_axis}\\n` +\n` Pain axis: ${inp.pain_axis}\\n` +\n` Stability axis: ${inp.stability_axis}\\n` +\n` Signal-Based Consideration: ${inp.signal_based_consideration}\\n` +\n` Solution type: ${inp.solution_type}\\n\\n` +\n`SIGNAL DETAIL:\\n` +\n` Emotion hypothesis: ${inp.emotion_hypothesis || 'Not available'}\\n` +\n` Keywords: ${inp.keywords || 'Not available'}\\n` +\n` Signal enrichment: ${inp.signal_enrichment_brief || 'Not available'}\\n\\n` +\n(inp.behavioral_interpretation ? `BEHAVIORAL CONTEXT: ${inp.behavioral_interpretation}\\n\\n` : '') +\n`Complete the response. Return plain text only. Your first line must be the opening sentence above.`;\n\nconst body_prompt_body = JSON.stringify({\n  model: 'claude-sonnet-4-6',\n  max_tokens: 500,\n  temperature: 0.3,\n  system: body_system_prompt,\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: body_user_prompt }]\n});\n\nreturn [{ json: {\n  bra_record_id: inp.bra_record_id,\n  confirmed_response_tier: inp.confirmed_response_tier,\n  governance_flag: inp.governance_flag,\n  human_review_required: inp.human_review_required,\n  solution_type: inp.solution_type,\n  emotional_axis: inp.emotional_axis,\n  pain_axis: inp.pain_axis,\n  stability_axis: inp.stability_axis,\n  signal_based_consideration: inp.signal_based_consideration,\n  tone_style: inp.tone_style,\n  urgency_level: inp.urgency_level,\n  commercial_risk_flag: inp.commercial_risk_flag,\n  behavioral_interpretation: inp.behavioral_interpretation,\n  lang: inp.lang,\n  client_id: inp.client_id,\n  enriched_emotion_tag: inp.enriched_emotion_tag,\n  enriched_pain_point: inp.enriched_pain_point,\n  pain_point_sub_category: inp.pain_point_sub_category,\n  signal_type: inp.signal_type,\n  intensity_level: inp.intensity_level,\n  hsi_record_id: inp.hsi_record_id,\n  ess_record_id: inp.ess_record_id,\n  eip_record_id: inp.eip_record_id,\n  ala_record_id: inp.ala_record_id,\n  prior_run_id: inp.prior_run_id,\n  reviewer_handle: inp.reviewer_handle,\n  emotion_hypothesis: inp.emotion_hypothesis,\n  keywords: inp.keywords,\n  brand_voice: inp.brand_voice,\n  brand_voice_brief: inp.brand_voice_brief,\n  signal_enrichment_brief: inp.signal_enrichment_brief,\n  lang_resolved: inp.lang_resolved,\n  opening_sentence: opening_sentence,\n  body_prompt_body: body_prompt_body\n} }];"
